        <type><ref refid="classthemis_1_1ingestion_1_1_deontic_extractor_1a90c47a450cd53b92ac564554ec2b02ab" kindref="member">DeonticExtractor::ExtractorFn</ref></type>
        <definition>DeonticExtractor::ExtractorFn themis::ingestion::LegalLlmAdapter::buildExtractorFn</definition>
        <argsstring>() const</argsstring>
        <name>buildExtractorFn</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::ingestion::LegalLlmAdapter::buildExtractorFn</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Build a <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1ingestion_1_1_deontic_extractor_1a90c47a450cd53b92ac564554ec2b02ab" kindref="member">DeonticExtractor::ExtractorFn</ref></computeroutput> for the configured model. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Phase 1: returns an empty <computeroutput>ExtractorFn{}</computeroutput> when no LLM is available. Callers should check <computeroutput>if (fn)</computeroutput> before passing to <computeroutput>setExtractorFn()</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>Phase 2: returns a callable that sends the text to the llama.cpp inference engine with a structured German legal extraction prompt and parses the JSON response into a <computeroutput><ref refid="structthemis_1_1ingestion_1_1_deontic_extraction" kindref="compound">DeonticExtraction</ref></computeroutput>.</para>
<para>Throws when a model path is explicitly configured but the file cannot be opened. This keeps misconfigured deployments fail-closed instead of silently degrading to regex extraction.</para>
<para>The returned function captures the model configuration by value so it remains valid independently of the <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1ingestion_1_1_legal_llm_adapter" kindref="compound">LegalLlmAdapter</ref></computeroutput> instance lifetime.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>ExtractorFn (may be empty in Phase 1 / when no model is set) </para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::runtime_error</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>if <computeroutput>config_.model_path</computeroutput> is set but the model file is not readable </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
